<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project name="Capacitive Touch for ULPSENSE" version="2.9.0.208">
    <desc><![CDATA[Demonstrates capacitive touch on LaunchPad with the ULP Sense BoosterPack (BOOSTXL-ULPSENSE), with processing.

The Sensor Controller samples the two capacitive touch areas on the ULP Sense BoosterPack, using the COMPA, ISRC and TDC peripherals.
The Sensor Controller processes the resulting TDC values in order to detect touch. Note that this touch detection algorithm is only an example of the Sensor Controller's processing capabilities, and should not be used in production.

The default sampling frequency is 32 Hz while touch is not detected, and ~100 Hz while touch is detected.

Touch detection is communicated to the System CPU application, which enables LEDs on the LaunchPad while touch is detected.

Task Testing should only be used for debugging purposes, as it will not run the Capacitive Touch task at the correct rate. Use Run-Time Logging for testing, performance evaluation and tuning.

BOOSTXL-ULPSENSE SETUP:
- Make sure that the supplied plexiglass is securely mounted over the capacitive touch buttons, without any air gaps.
- Remove all jumpers

See the header in the application source file ("main_tirtos.c") for further details and instructions. This file is located in the source code output directory.]]></desc>
